{
 "encounter_id": "00758",
 "speakers": {
  "person_1": "PATIENT",
  "person_2": "DOCTOR"
 },
 "turns": [
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Hello. It's my chest again, doctor. I think it's playing up. More than usual."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Tell me what's different from your usual."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "I'm coughing up more, a lot more. And it's gone yellowy green. Usually it's clear, or a bit white."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "How long has it been like this?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "A week, nearly. Since last Wednesday."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "How much are you bringing up in a day, would you say?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Half a cupful, maybe. In the morning, mostly."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Have you had a fever, or night sweats?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "No fever, I haven't felt hot."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Any blood in the phlegm?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "No blood. It's just yellow and thick."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "And breathless, more than usual?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "A bit, on the stairs. Not at rest."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "You've had bronchiectasis for a while, haven't you? ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Since my thirties. And my chest's been bad since the pneumonia. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Any operations?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Just my adenoids, when I was small, I think. Or maybe my tonsils."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Let me check your pulse and oxygen, and have a listen. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Right. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Pulse 88, oxygen 95 percent, temperature 36.9.",
   "pause": 12.0
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Is that low? ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "It's a touch lower than I'd like, but typical for you. Breathe in and out.",
   "pause": 18.0
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Is it crackly? ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Yes, crackles at the bottom of both lungs, and a bit of wheeze."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "What does it mean? ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "A change in your phlegm to yellow-green, more of it, and more breathlessness, fits a flare-up of your bronchiectasis, probably a chest infection on top."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "What happens now? ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "I'd like to send a sample of your phlegm to the lab, to see which germ is growing."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "And then? ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "The result will come back to the practice and we'll get it to you. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Keep up your daily physiotherapy, the breathing exercises that clear the phlegm, twice a day, and drink plenty of fluids."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "I haven't been doing them as much as I should. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Please do, it makes a big difference in a flare-up. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Okay. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "If you get breathless at rest, cough up blood, develop a high temperature, or feel confused, come back or call 999."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Right. Thanks, doctor. ~"
  }
 ],
